IMPORT `ccc28-part24-s752`
IMPORT `ccc28-part24a-dangerous-offender`

-- ccc28-part24b-long-term.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), sections 753.1 to 755 (PART XXIV, Dangerous Offenders and Long-term Offenders):
-- long-term offenders, long-term supervision, the hearing of an application, and the exception for a life sentence. Layer 1 of part ccc28.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); it is not the
-- official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- READING A RESULT: as in ccc28-part24a-dangerous-offender.l4. JUST FALSE where the text says no in its own words; NOTHING where it is silent or
-- limited by its own wording; the court's own judgments ("satisfied", "of the opinion") are inputs.

§ `Part XXIV, section 753.1: long-term offenders`

-- (1) "The court may, on application made under this Part following the filing of an assessment report under subsection 752.1(2), find an offender to be a
-- long-term offender if it is satisfied that (a) ...; (b) ...; and (c) ...". A power ("may"). Two gates: "on application ... following the filing" (an "on"
-- gate: JUST FALSE, listed in NOTES.md group (i)); "if it is satisfied that" (an "if" gate on a power: NOTHING, fork F3).
-- src:16444 | 753.1 (1) The court may, on application made under this Part following the filing of an assessment report under subsection 752.1(2), find an offender to be a long-term offender if it is satisfied that
-- src:16445 | (a) it would be appropriate to impose a sentence of imprisonment of two years or more for the offence for which the offender has been convicted;
-- src:16446 | (b) there is a substantial risk that the offender will reoffend; and
-- src:16447 | (c) there is a reasonable possibility of eventual control of the risk in the community.
@ref s 753.1(1) (src:16444-16447)
GIVEN `an application was made under this Part following the filing of an assessment report under subsection 752.1(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that it would be appropriate to impose a sentence of imprisonment of two years or more for the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that there is a substantial risk that the offender will reoffend` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that there is a reasonable possibility of eventual control of the risk in the community` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 753.1(1) the court may find the offender to be a long-term offender` MEANS
    IF NOT `an application was made under this Part following the filing of an assessment report under subsection 752.1(2)`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on application made under this Part following the filing of an assessment report under subsection 752.1(2)"
    ELSE IF     `the court is satisfied that it would be appropriate to impose a sentence of imprisonment of two years or more for the offence`
            AND `the court is satisfied that there is a substantial risk that the offender will reoffend`
            AND `the court is satisfied that there is a reasonable possibility of eventual control of the risk in the community`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if it is satisfied that": a grant limited by an "if" gate; the text does not say the court may not find the offender to be a long-term offender otherwise

-- (2)(a) "the offender has been convicted of an offence under section 151, 152, ... or 286.3(2) ..., or has engaged in serious conduct of a sexual nature in the
-- commission of another offence of which the offender has been convicted". The provisions, one entry per provision the paragraph names; the subsection "" is the
-- whole section. This is the answer s 752.1(1) asks for as "an offence referred to in paragraph 753.1(2)(a)".
-- src:16450 | (a) the offender has been convicted of an offence under section 151 (sexual interference),152 (invitation to sexual touching or exposure), 153 (sexual exploitation), 153.1 (sexual exploitation of person with disability), 163.1 (child sexual abuse and exploitation material), 170 (parent or guardian procuring sexual activity), 171 (householder permitting sexual activity), 171.1 (making sexually explicit material available to child), 172.1 (luring a child) or 172.2 (agreement or arrangement — sexual offence against child), subsection 173(2) (exposure) or section 271 (sexual assault), 272 (sexual assault with a weapon), 273 (aggravated sexual assault) or 279.011 (trafficking — person under 18 years) or subsection 279.02(2) (material benefit — trafficking of person under 18 years), 279.03(2) (withholding or destroying documents — trafficking of person under 18 years), 286.1(2) (obtaining sexual services for consideration from person under 18 years), 286.2(2) (material benefit from sexual services provided by person under 18 years) or 286.3(2) (procuring — person under 18 years), or has engaged in serious conduct of a sexual nature in the commission of another offence of which the offender has been convicted; and
@ref s 753.1(2)(a) (src:16450)
`s 753.1(2)(a) the listed provisions` MEANS
    LIST
        (`Provision of the Code` OF 151, "")           -- section 151 (sexual interference)
      , (`Provision of the Code` OF 152, "")           -- section 152 (invitation to sexual touching or exposure)
      , (`Provision of the Code` OF 153, "")           -- section 153 (sexual exploitation)
      , (`Provision of the Code` OF 153.1, "")         -- section 153.1 (sexual exploitation of person with disability)
      , (`Provision of the Code` OF 163.1, "")         -- section 163.1 (child sexual abuse and exploitation material)
      , (`Provision of the Code` OF 170, "")           -- section 170 (parent or guardian procuring sexual activity)
      , (`Provision of the Code` OF 171, "")           -- section 171 (householder permitting sexual activity)
      , (`Provision of the Code` OF 171.1, "")         -- section 171.1 (making sexually explicit material available to child)
      , (`Provision of the Code` OF 172.1, "")         -- section 172.1 (luring a child)
      , (`Provision of the Code` OF 172.2, "")         -- section 172.2 (agreement or arrangement -- sexual offence against child)
      , (`Provision of the Code` OF 173, "(2)")        -- subsection 173(2) (exposure)
      , (`Provision of the Code` OF 271, "")           -- section 271 (sexual assault)
      , (`Provision of the Code` OF 272, "")           -- section 272 (sexual assault with a weapon)
      , (`Provision of the Code` OF 273, "")           -- section 273 (aggravated sexual assault)
      , (`Provision of the Code` OF 279.011, "")       -- section 279.011 (trafficking -- person under 18 years)
      , (`Provision of the Code` OF 279.02, "(2)")     -- subsection 279.02(2) (material benefit -- trafficking of person under 18 years)
      , (`Provision of the Code` OF 279.03, "(2)")     -- subsection 279.03(2) (withholding or destroying documents -- trafficking of person under 18 years)
      , (`Provision of the Code` OF 286.1, "(2)")      -- subsection 286.1(2) (obtaining sexual services for consideration from person under 18 years)
      , (`Provision of the Code` OF 286.2, "(2)")      -- subsection 286.2(2) (material benefit from sexual services provided by person under 18 years)
      , (`Provision of the Code` OF 286.3, "(2)")      -- subsection 286.3(2) (procuring -- person under 18 years)

-- Whether the offence is one the paragraph names: the provisions of this Act as it now reads, for the offence itself. (The paragraph speaks of "an offence
-- under" the listed provisions; an attempt or a conspiracy is not "an offence under" them, and the paragraph is silent about one: NOTHING.)
GIVEN offence IS A `s 752 offence`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 753.1(2)(a) the offence is one the paragraph names` MEANS
    IF     offence's `s 752 source` EQUALS `s 752 an offence under this Act as it now reads`
       AND `s 752 the provision is in the list` (offence's `s 752 provision`) `s 753.1(2)(a) the listed provisions`
    THEN CONSIDER offence's `s 752 implication`
         WHEN `s 752 convicted of the offence itself` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 752 convicted of an attempt to commit the offence` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph names "an offence under" the provisions, and says nothing of an attempt
         WHEN `s 752 convicted of a conspiracy to commit the offence` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph names "an offence under" the provisions, and says nothing of a conspiracy
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "has been convicted of an offence under section 151 (sexual interference),152 (invitation to sexual touching or exposure), 153 (sexual exploitation)"

-- "The court shall be satisfied that there is a substantial risk that the offender will reoffend if (a) ... and (b) the offender (i) has shown a pattern of
-- repetitive behaviour, ... or (ii) by conduct in any sexual matter ..., has shown a likelihood of causing injury, pain or other evil to other persons in the
-- future through similar offences."  A deeming of the court's satisfaction ("shall be satisfied ... if"): a failed "if" is read as the text's no, within this
-- subsection (marginal reading (a)); the other reading is that the court may be satisfied on other grounds (NOTHING).
-- src:16449 | (2) The court shall be satisfied that there is a substantial risk that the offender will reoffend if
-- src:16451 | (b) the offender
-- src:16452 | (i) has shown a pattern of repetitive behaviour, of which the offence for which he or she has been convicted forms a part, that shows a likelihood of the offender’s causing death or injury to other persons or inflicting severe psychological damage on other persons, or
-- src:16453 | (ii) by conduct in any sexual matter including that involved in the commission of the offence for which the offender has been convicted, has shown a likelihood of causing injury, pain or other evil to other persons in the future through similar offences.
@ref s 753.1(2) (src:16449-16453)
GIVEN offence IS A `s 752 offence`
      `the offender has engaged in serious conduct of a sexual nature in the commission of another offence of which the offender has been convicted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offender has shown a pattern of repetitive behaviour, of which the offence forms a part, that shows a likelihood of causing death or injury to other persons or inflicting severe psychological damage on other persons (b)(i)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offender, by conduct in any sexual matter, has shown a likelihood of causing injury, pain or other evil to other persons in the future through similar offences (b)(ii)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 753.1(2) the court shall be satisfied that there is a substantial risk that the offender will reoffend` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 752 both hold` `paragraph (a) holds` (JUST `paragraph (b) holds`)
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The court shall be satisfied that there is a substantial risk that the offender will reoffend if"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (a) names "an offence under" the provisions, and the offender's conviction is for an attempt or a conspiracy
    WHERE
        `paragraph (a) holds` MEANS
            `s 752 either holds`
                (`s 753.1(2)(a) the offence is one the paragraph names` offence)
                (JUST `the offender has engaged in serious conduct of a sexual nature in the commission of another offence of which the offender has been convicted`)
        `paragraph (b) holds` MEANS
                `the offender has shown a pattern of repetitive behaviour, of which the offence forms a part, that shows a likelihood of causing death or injury to other persons or inflicting severe psychological damage on other persons (b)(i)`
            OR `the offender, by conduct in any sexual matter, has shown a likelihood of causing injury, pain or other evil to other persons in the future through similar offences (b)(ii)`

-- (3) "If the court finds an offender to be a long-term offender, it shall (a) impose a sentence for the offence ..., which must be a minimum punishment of
-- imprisonment for a term of two years; and (b) order that the offender be subject to long-term supervision for a period that does not exceed 10 years."
-- src:16455 | (3) If the court finds an offender to be a long-term offender, it shall
-- src:16456 | (a) impose a sentence for the offence for which the offender has been convicted, which must be a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of two years; and
-- src:16457 | (b) order that the offender be subject to long-term supervision for a period that does not exceed 10 years.
@ref s 753.1(3) (src:16455-16457)
GIVEN `the court has found the offender to be a long-term offender` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the term of imprisonment imposed for the offence` IS A `Length of time`
      `the period of long-term supervision ordered` IS A `Length of time`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 753.1(3) the sentence and order are within paragraphs (a) and (b)` MEANS
    IF NOT `the court has found the offender to be a long-term offender`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the court finds an offender to be a long-term offender"
    ELSE IF NOT `s 752 the length of time is at least` `the term of imprisonment imposed for the offence` `two years`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "which must be a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of two years"
         ELSE IF NOT `s 752 the length of time is at least` `ten years` `the period of long-term supervision ordered`
              THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for a period that does not exceed 10 years"
              ELSE JUST TRUE

-- (3.1) "The court may not impose a sentence under paragraph (3)(a) and the sentence that was imposed for the offence for which the offender was convicted
-- stands despite the offender's being found to be a long-term offender, if the application was one that (a) was made after the offender begins to serve the
-- sentence in a case to which paragraphs 753(2)(a) and (b) apply; and (b) was treated as an application under this section further to the court deciding to
-- do so under paragraph 753(5)(a)."  A bar ("may not ... if"): a failed "if" is the text's no (marginal reading (a)).
-- src:16458 | Exception — if application made after sentencing
-- src:16459 | (3.1) The court may not impose a sentence under paragraph (3)(a) and the sentence that was imposed for the offence for which the offender was convicted stands despite the offender’s being found to be a long-term offender, if the application was one that
-- src:16460 | (a) was made after the offender begins to serve the sentence in a case to which paragraphs 753(2)(a) and (b) apply; and
-- src:16461 | (b) was treated as an application under this section further to the court deciding to do so under paragraph 753(5)(a).
@ref s 753.1(3.1) (src:16458-16461)
GIVEN `the application was made after the offender begins to serve the sentence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraphs (2)(a) and (b) of section 753 apply, by s 753(2)(a) and (b)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the application was treated as an application under this section further to the court deciding to do so under paragraph 753(5)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 753.1(3.1) the court may not impose a sentence under paragraph (3)(a)` MEANS
    IF NOT `the application was made after the offender begins to serve the sentence`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the application was one that (a) was made after the offender begins to serve the sentence"
    ELSE IF NOT `the application was treated as an application under this section further to the court deciding to do so under paragraph 753(5)(a)`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) was treated as an application under this section further to the court deciding to do so under paragraph 753(5)(a)"
         ELSE CONSIDER `paragraphs (2)(a) and (b) of section 753 apply, by s 753(2)(a) and (b)`
              WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in a case to which paragraphs 753(2)(a) and (b) apply"
              WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the answer of paragraphs 753(2)(a) and (b) is itself not covered

-- (6) "If the court does not find an offender to be a long-term offender, the court shall impose sentence for the offence for which the offender has been convicted."
-- src:16463 | If offender not found to be long-term offender
-- src:16464 | (6) If the court does not find an offender to be a long-term offender, the court shall impose sentence for the offence for which the offender has been convicted.
@ref s 753.1(6) (src:16463-16464)
GIVEN `the court does not find the offender to be a long-term offender` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 753.1(6) the court shall impose sentence for the offence` MEANS
    IF `the court does not find the offender to be a long-term offender`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the court does not find an offender to be a long-term offender"

§ `Part XXIV, section 753.2: long-term supervision`

-- (1) "Subject to subsection (2), an offender who is subject to long-term supervision shall be supervised in the community in accordance with the Corrections and
-- Conditional Release Act when the offender has finished serving (a) the sentence for the offence ...; and (b) all other sentences for offences for which the offender
-- is convicted and for which sentence of a term of imprisonment is imposed on the offender, either before or after the conviction for the offence referred to in paragraph (a)."
-- src:16466 | 753.2 (1) Subject to subsection (2), an offender who is subject to long-term supervision shall be supervised in the community in accordance with the Corrections and Conditional Release Act when the offender has finished serving
-- src:16467 | (a) the sentence for the offence for which the offender has been convicted; and
-- src:16468 | (b) all other sentences for offences for which the offender is convicted and for which sentence of a term of imprisonment is imposed on the offender, either before or after the conviction for the offence referred to in paragraph (a).
@ref s 753.2(1) (src:16466-16468)
GIVEN `the offender is subject to long-term supervision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offender has finished serving the sentence for the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offender has finished serving all other sentences of a term of imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 753.2(1) the offender shall be supervised in the community` MEANS
    IF NOT `the offender is subject to long-term supervision`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an offender who is subject to long-term supervision": the duty is limited to a named class, and the section is silent about any other offender
    ELSE IF     `the offender has finished serving the sentence for the offence`
            AND `the offender has finished serving all other sentences of a term of imprisonment`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "when the offender has finished serving"

-- (2) "A sentence imposed on an offender referred to in subsection (1), other than a sentence that requires imprisonment, is to be served concurrently with the
-- long-term supervision."  The exception ("other than a sentence that requires imprisonment") is a limit by the subsection's own wording: for a sentence that requires
-- imprisonment the subsection is silent (fork F5).
-- src:16470 | (2) A sentence imposed on an offender referred to in subsection (1), other than a sentence that requires imprisonment, is to be served concurrently with the long-term supervision.
@ref s 753.2(2) (src:16470)
GIVEN `the sentence is imposed on an offender referred to in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sentence requires imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 753.2(2) the sentence is to be served concurrently with the long-term supervision` MEANS
    IF NOT `the sentence is imposed on an offender referred to in subsection (1)`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A sentence imposed on an offender referred to in subsection (1)"
    ELSE IF `the sentence requires imprisonment`
         THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "other than a sentence that requires imprisonment"
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- (3) "An offender who is required to be supervised, a member of the Parole Board of Canada or, on approval of that Board, the offender's parole supervisor, ... may apply to
-- a superior court of criminal jurisdiction for an order reducing the period of long-term supervision or terminating it on the ground that the offender no longer presents a
-- substantial risk of reoffending and thereby being a danger to the community."  A power ("may") with named applicants, a named court and a named ground: outside the names,
-- the text is silent (NOTHING); "on approval of that Board" is an "on" gate on the parole supervisor (JUST FALSE, listed in NOTES.md group (i)).
DECLARE `s 753.2(3) applicant` IS ONE OF
    `s 753.2(3) the offender who is required to be supervised`
    `s 753.2(3) a member of the Parole Board of Canada`
    `s 753.2(3) the offender's parole supervisor with the approval of the Parole Board of Canada`
    `s 753.2(3) the offender's parole supervisor without the approval of the Parole Board of Canada`
    `s 753.2(3) any other person`

-- src:16472 | (3) An offender who is required to be supervised, a member of the Parole Board of Canada or, on approval of that Board, the offender’s parole supervisor, as defined in subsection 99(1) of the Corrections and Conditional Release Act, may apply to a superior court of criminal jurisdiction for an order reducing the period of long-term supervision or terminating it on the ground that the offender no longer presents a substantial risk of reoffending and thereby being a danger to the community. The onus of proving that ground is on the applicant.
@ref s 753.2(3) (src:16472)
GIVEN applicant IS A `s 753.2(3) applicant`
      `s 2 superior court of criminal jurisdiction: the court applied to is a superior court of criminal jurisdiction` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the ground is that the offender no longer presents a substantial risk of reoffending and thereby being a danger to the community` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 753.2(3) the applicant may apply for an order reducing or terminating the period of long-term supervision` MEANS
    CONSIDER applicant
    WHEN `s 753.2(3) the offender who is required to be supervised` THEN `the ground and the court`
    WHEN `s 753.2(3) a member of the Parole Board of Canada` THEN `the ground and the court`
    WHEN `s 753.2(3) the offender's parole supervisor with the approval of the Parole Board of Canada` THEN `the ground and the court`
    WHEN `s 753.2(3) the offender's parole supervisor without the approval of the Parole Board of Canada` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on approval of that Board, the offender's parole supervisor"
    WHEN `s 753.2(3) any other person` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection names the persons who may apply, and does not say that no one else may
    WHERE
        `the ground and the court` MEANS
            IF NOT `the ground is that the offender no longer presents a substantial risk of reoffending and thereby being a danger to the community`
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on the ground that the offender no longer presents a substantial risk of reoffending and thereby being a danger to the community": the subsection names this ground, and does not say that no other ground may be put
            ELSE CONSIDER `s 2 superior court of criminal jurisdiction: the court applied to is a superior court of criminal jurisdiction`
                 WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
                 WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to a superior court of criminal jurisdiction": the subsection names the court, and says nothing of an application to another court
                 WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the answer of s 2 "superior court of criminal jurisdiction" is itself not covered

-- "The onus of proving that ground is on the applicant."
-- src:16472 | (3) An offender who is required to be supervised, a member of the Parole Board of Canada or, on approval of that Board, the offender’s parole supervisor, as defined in subsection 99(1) of the Corrections and Conditional Release Act, may apply to a superior court of criminal jurisdiction for an order reducing the period of long-term supervision or terminating it on the ground that the offender no longer presents a substantial risk of reoffending and thereby being a danger to the community. The onus of proving that ground is on the applicant.
@ref s 753.2(3) (src:16472)
GIVEN `the application is made under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 753.2(3) the onus of proving the ground is on the applicant` MEANS
    IF `the application is made under subsection (3)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The onus of proving that ground is on the applicant": the sentence speaks of an application under subsection (3), and is silent about any other

-- (4) "The applicant must give notice of an application under subsection (3) to the Attorney General at the time the application is made."
DECLARE `s 753.2(4) party` IS ONE OF
    `s 753.2(4) the applicant`

DECLARE `s 753.2(4) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 753.2(4) give notice of the application to the Attorney General`

-- src:16474 | (4) The applicant must give notice of an application under subsection (3) to the Attorney General at the time the application is made.
@ref s 753.2(4) (src:16474)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 753.2(4) party` `s 753.2(4) action`
`s 753.2(4) the duty of the applicant to give notice to the Attorney General` MEANS
    PARTY `s 753.2(4) the applicant`
    MUST `s 753.2(4) give notice of the application to the Attorney General`
    WITHIN 0
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 753.2(4) the applicant` BECAUSE "the applicant did not give notice of the application to the Attorney General at the time the application was made"

@ref s 753.2(4) (src:16474)
GIVEN `the date the application was made` IS A DATE
      `the date the notice was given` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 753.2(4) the notice is given at the time the application is made` MEANS
    IF Day `the date the notice was given` EQUALS Day `the date the application was made`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "at the time the application is made"

§ `Part XXIV, section 753.3: breach of long-term supervision`

-- (1) "An offender who, without reasonable excuse, fails or refuses to comply with long-term supervision is guilty of (a) an indictable offence and liable to
-- imprisonment for a term of not more than 10 years; or (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction."  An offence-creating provision: each element is a
-- named class or a "without" clause, so a case outside the elements is not covered (NOTHING, fork F6; the other reading is JUST FALSE).
-- src:16476 | 753.3 (1) An offender who, without reasonable excuse, fails or refuses to comply with long-term supervision is guilty of
-- src:16477 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 10 years; or
-- src:16478 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 753.3(1) (src:16476-16478)
GIVEN `the offender is subject to long-term supervision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offender fails or refuses to comply with long-term supervision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offender has a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 753.3(1) the offender is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the offender is subject to long-term supervision` AND `the offender fails or refuses to comply with long-term supervision`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An offender who ... fails or refuses to comply with long-term supervision is guilty of": the provision names the conduct, and says nothing of other conduct
    ELSE IF `the offender has a reasonable excuse`
         THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "without reasonable excuse": the offence is limited by a "without" clause, and the provision is silent about an offender who has a reasonable excuse
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- The two limbs of the penalty: (a) indictable, imprisonment for not more than 10 years; (b) summary conviction, for which no punishment is stated here.
GIVEN mode IS A `Mode of proceeding`
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 753.3(1) the punishment` MEANS
    CONSIDER mode
    WHEN `by indictment` THEN Punishment OF `by indictment`, (`imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`), `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`   -- (a) "liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 10 years"
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN Punishment OF `on summary conviction`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`   -- (b) states no punishment: not covered here

-- (2) "An accused who is charged with an offence under subsection (1) may be tried and punished by any court having jurisdiction to try that offence in the place where
-- the offence is alleged to have been committed or in the place where the accused is found, is arrested or is in custody, but if the place where the accused is found, is
-- arrested or is in custody is outside the province in which the offence is alleged to have been committed, no proceedings in respect of that offence shall be instituted in
-- that place without the consent of the Attorney General of that province."  A power with named places (outside them: silent) and a bar ("without the consent").
DECLARE `s 753.3(2) place` IS ONE OF
    `s 753.3(2) the place where the offence is alleged to have been committed`
    `s 753.3(2) the place where the accused is found, is arrested or is in custody, within the province in which the offence is alleged to have been committed`
    `s 753.3(2) the place where the accused is found, is arrested or is in custody, outside the province in which the offence is alleged to have been committed`
    `s 753.3(2) any other place`

-- src:16480 | (2) An accused who is charged with an offence under subsection (1) may be tried and punished by any court having jurisdiction to try that offence in the place where the offence is alleged to have been committed or in the place where the accused is found, is arrested or is in custody, but if the place where the accused is found, is arrested or is in custody is outside the province in which the offence is alleged to have been committed, no proceedings in respect of that offence shall be instituted in that place without the consent of the Attorney General of that province.
@ref s 753.3(2) (src:16480)
GIVEN `the accused is charged with an offence under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court has jurisdiction to try that offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      place IS A `s 753.3(2) place`
      `the Attorney General of that province has consented` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 753.3(2) the accused may be tried and punished in this place` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the accused is charged with an offence under subsection (1)` AND `the court has jurisdiction to try that offence`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An accused who is charged with an offence under subsection (1) may be tried and punished by any court having jurisdiction to try that offence"
    ELSE CONSIDER place
         WHEN `s 753.3(2) the place where the offence is alleged to have been committed` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 753.3(2) the place where the accused is found, is arrested or is in custody, within the province in which the offence is alleged to have been committed` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 753.3(2) the place where the accused is found, is arrested or is in custody, outside the province in which the offence is alleged to have been committed` THEN
             IF `the Attorney General of that province has consented`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no proceedings in respect of that offence shall be instituted in that place without the consent of the Attorney General of that province"
         WHEN `s 753.3(2) any other place` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection names the places where the accused may be tried, and does not say that no other place will do

§ `Part XXIV, section 753.4: a new offence while subject to long-term supervision`

-- (1) "If an offender who is subject to long-term supervision commits one or more offences under this or any other Act and a court imposes a sentence of imprisonment
-- for the offence or offences, the long-term supervision is interrupted until the offender has finished serving all the sentences, unless the court orders its termination."
-- "unless the court orders its termination": once the court has so ordered, the supervision is not interrupted (fork F7: JUST FALSE for the interruption; the other reading is
-- that the subsection is then silent about the supervision).
-- src:16482 | 753.4 (1) If an offender who is subject to long-term supervision commits one or more offences under this or any other Act and a court imposes a sentence of imprisonment for the offence or offences, the long-term supervision is interrupted until the offender has finished serving all the sentences, unless the court orders its termination.
@ref s 753.4(1) (src:16482)
GIVEN `the offender is subject to long-term supervision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offender commits one or more offences under this or any other Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a court imposes a sentence of imprisonment for the offence or offences` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offender has finished serving all the sentences` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court orders the termination of the long-term supervision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 753.4(1) the long-term supervision is interrupted` MEANS
    IF NOT (    `the offender is subject to long-term supervision`
            AND `the offender commits one or more offences under this or any other Act`
            AND `a court imposes a sentence of imprisonment for the offence or offences`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an offender who is subject to long-term supervision commits one or more offences under this or any other Act and a court imposes a sentence of imprisonment for the offence or offences"
    ELSE IF `the court orders the termination of the long-term supervision`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the court orders its termination"
         ELSE IF `the offender has finished serving all the sentences`
              THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "until the offender has finished serving all the sentences"
              ELSE JUST TRUE

-- (2) "A court that imposes a sentence of imprisonment under subsection (1) may order a reduction in the length of the period of the offender's long-term supervision."
-- A power ("may"); "that imposes a sentence of imprisonment under subsection (1)" describes the court (a named class).
-- src:16484 | (2) A court that imposes a sentence of imprisonment under subsection (1) may order a reduction in the length of the period of the offender’s long-term supervision.
@ref s 753.4(2) (src:16484)
GIVEN `the court imposes a sentence of imprisonment under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 753.4(2) the court may order a reduction in the length of the period of long-term supervision` MEANS
    IF `the court imposes a sentence of imprisonment under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A court that imposes a sentence of imprisonment under subsection (1)": the power is given to a named class of court, and the subsection is silent about any other

§ `Part XXIV, section 754: hearing of an application`

-- (1) "With the exception of an application for remand for assessment, the court may not hear an application made under this Part unless (a) the Attorney General of
-- the province in which the offender was tried has, either before or after the making of the application, consented to the application; (b) at least seven days notice has
-- been given to the offender by the prosecutor, following the making of the application, outlining the basis on which it is intended to found the application; and (c) a
-- copy of the notice has been filed with the clerk of the court or the provincial court judge, as the case may be."  A bar ("may not ... unless"): the text's no when the
-- exception does not apply and a paragraph is unmet; the exception and the satisfied "unless" both lift it (fork F8: the exception answers JUST FALSE).
-- src:16486 | 754 (1) With the exception of an application for remand for assessment, the court may not hear an application made under this Part unless
-- src:16487 | (a) the Attorney General of the province in which the offender was tried has, either before or after the making of the application, consented to the application;
-- src:16488 | (b) at least seven days notice has been given to the offender by the prosecutor, following the making of the application, outlining the basis on which it is intended to found the application; and
-- src:16489 | (c) a copy of the notice has been filed with the clerk of the court or the provincial court judge, as the case may be.
@ref s 754(1) (src:16486-16489)
GIVEN `the application is an application for remand for assessment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Attorney General of the province in which the offender was tried has consented to the application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of days of notice given to the offender by the prosecutor` IS A NUMBER
      `the notice was given following the making of the application and outlined the basis on which it is intended to found the application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a copy of the notice has been filed with the clerk of the court or the provincial court judge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 754(1) the court may not hear the application` MEANS
    IF `the application is an application for remand for assessment`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "With the exception of an application for remand for assessment"
    ELSE IF     `the Attorney General of the province in which the offender was tried has consented to the application`
            AND `the number of days of notice given to the offender by the prosecutor` AT LEAST 7
            AND `the notice was given following the making of the application and outlined the basis on which it is intended to found the application`
            AND `a copy of the notice has been filed with the clerk of the court or the provincial court judge`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the court may not hear an application made under this Part unless"
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- (2) "An application under this Part shall be heard and determined by the court without a jury."
-- src:16491 | (2) An application under this Part shall be heard and determined by the court without a jury.
@ref s 754(2) (src:16491)
GIVEN `the application is heard and determined by the court without a jury` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 754(2) the application is heard and determined by the court without a jury` MEANS
    IF `the application is heard and determined by the court without a jury`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be heard and determined by the court without a jury"

-- (3) "For the purposes of an application under this Part, where an offender admits any allegations contained in the notice referred to in paragraph (1)(b), no proof of
-- those allegations is required."
-- src:16493 | (3) For the purposes of an application under this Part, where an offender admits any allegations contained in the notice referred to in paragraph (1)(b), no proof of those allegations is required.
@ref s 754(3) (src:16493)
GIVEN `the offender admits the allegations contained in the notice referred to in paragraph (1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 754(3) no proof of the allegations is required` MEANS
    IF `the offender admits the allegations contained in the notice referred to in paragraph (1)(b)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where an offender admits any allegations contained in the notice referred to in paragraph (1)(b)"

-- (4) "The production of a document purporting to contain any nomination or consent that may be made or given by the Attorney General under this Part and purporting to be
-- signed by the Attorney General is, in the absence of any evidence to the contrary, proof of that nomination or consent without proof of the signature or the official
-- character of the person appearing to have signed the document."
-- src:16495 | (4) The production of a document purporting to contain any nomination or consent that may be made or given by the Attorney General under this Part and purporting to be signed by the Attorney General is, in the absence of any evidence to the contrary, proof of that nomination or consent without proof of the signature or the official character of the person appearing to have signed the document.
@ref s 754(4) (src:16495)
GIVEN `a document is produced that purports to contain a nomination or consent that may be made or given by the Attorney General under this Part and purports to be signed by the Attorney General` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is evidence to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 754(4) the document is proof of the nomination or consent` MEANS
    IF NOT `a document is produced that purports to contain a nomination or consent that may be made or given by the Attorney General under this Part and purports to be signed by the Attorney General`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a document purporting to contain any nomination or consent ... and purporting to be signed by the Attorney General": the subsection speaks of such a document, and is silent about any other
    ELSE IF `there is evidence to the contrary`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the absence of any evidence to the contrary"
         ELSE JUST TRUE

§ `Part XXIV, section 755: exception to long-term supervision, life sentence`

-- (1) "The court shall not order that an offender be subject to long-term supervision if they have been sentenced to life imprisonment."
-- src:16497 | 755 (1) The court shall not order that an offender be subject to long-term supervision if they have been sentenced to life imprisonment.
@ref s 755(1) (src:16497)
GIVEN `the offender has been sentenced to life imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 755(1) the court shall not order that the offender be subject to long-term supervision` MEANS
    IF `the offender has been sentenced to life imprisonment`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if they have been sentenced to life imprisonment"

-- (2) "The periods of long-term supervision to which an offender is subject at any particular time must not total more than 10 years."
-- The periods are stated as lengths of time (years, months, days). A month is not a fixed number of days, so a total in days is read as between 28 and 31 days to the month
-- (fork F9): the total is not more than 10 years in every calendar when 28 times the whole months plus the days is at most 3360, and is more than 10 years in every calendar
-- when 31 times the whole months plus the days is above 3720; between the two, the text does not settle it (NOTHING).
-- src:16499 | (2) The periods of long-term supervision to which an offender is subject at any particular time must not total more than 10 years.
@ref s 755(2) (src:16499)
GIVEN periods IS A LIST OF `Length of time`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 755(2) the total number of whole months of the periods` MEANS sum (map `s 752 the whole months in the length of time` periods)

GIVEN periods IS A LIST OF `Length of time`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 755(2) the total number of days of the periods` MEANS sum (map `s 752 the days in the length of time` periods)

@ref s 755(2) (src:16499)
GIVEN periods IS A LIST OF `Length of time`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 755(2) the periods of long-term supervision do not total more than 10 years` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (28 TIMES `s 755(2) the total number of whole months of the periods` periods) PLUS `s 755(2) the total number of days of the periods` periods AT MOST 3360 THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (31 TIMES `s 755(2) the total number of whole months of the periods` periods) PLUS `s 755(2) the total number of days of the periods` periods GREATER THAN 3720
            THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not total more than 10 years"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): whether the days make a month more than 10 years depends on the calendar, which the subsection does not fix
